    "detailed_description": "Let's solve a scrambled cube in its unfolded state. Manipulate the cube pieces of a randomly mixed cube to solve it.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2878050/extras/6c8cb015ddc78b01faf8a4aac1fe2b62.poster.avif?t=1718377535\" width=400 height=400 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2878050/extras/6c8cb015ddc78b01faf8a4aac1fe2b62.webm?t=1718377535\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2878050/extras/6c8cb015ddc78b01faf8a4aac1fe2b62.mp4?t=1718377535\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>Pressing the button briefly will cause the cube to be shuffled a set number of times.<br><br>If you keep holding down the mouse button, the timer won't start, allowing you up to 15 seconds of inspection time to examine the shuffled cube.<br><br>Releasing the mouse button or moving away from it will start the timer and initiate the cube solving process.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2878050/extras/d1fbcd7b6651ab87446ed937abe9b59c.poster.avif?t=1718377535\" width=400 height=400 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2878050/extras/d1fbcd7b6651ab87446ed937abe9b59c.webm?t=1718377535\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2878050/extras/d1fbcd7b6651ab87446ed937abe9b59c.mp4?t=1718377535\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>Click on a cube piece and manipulate it by dragging up, down, left, or right to complete the cube.<br><br>After solving the cube, the attempt number and the time taken by the timer will be recorded.<br>Additionally, you can choose to forfeit the attempt by pressing the button.<br><br>In the demo version, you can play with a 3x3x3 cube and three different nets.",
